@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Provisioning Account Partner Integration
	Testing to assure that koroneiki account partner information transfers properly to the account details page.

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I tear down the teams on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Partner |
	| Updated Partner   |
	* I tear down the team roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Partner |
	* I tear down the external links for the product "Liferay DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following entity id values
	| Liferay DXP Production |
	* I tear down the external links for the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following entity id values
	| Platinum Subscription |
	* I tear down the external links for the product "Gold Subscription" on koroneiki with the following entity id values
	| Gold Subscription |
	* I tear down the external links for the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" on koroneiki with the following entity id and domain values
	| ${staticDossieraAccountKey}   | salesforce |
	| ${staticDossieraAccountKey}   | dossiera   |
	| ${staticSalesforceProjectKey} | salesforce |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Vchild - ${staticCompanyName}" for the following products
	| Liferay DXP Production |
	| Platinum Subscription  |
	| Gold Subscription      |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Pchild - ${staticCompanyName}" for the following products
	| Liferay DXP Production |
	| Platinum Subscription  |
	| Gold Subscription      |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" for the following products
	| Liferay DXP Production |
	| Platinum Subscription  |
	| Gold Subscription      |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Onepro - ${staticCompanyName}" for the following products
	| Liferay DXP Production |
	| Platinum Subscription  |
	| Gold Subscription      |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Korpar - ${staticCompanyName}" for the following products
	| Service Partnership              |
	| Basic Reseller Partnership       |
	| Value-Added Reseller Partnership |
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| Platinum Subscription      |
	| Gold Subscription          |
	| Service Partnership        |
	| Basic Reseller Partnership |
	* I tear down the contact roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Liferay Account Customer Role |
 	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| KORPARKORPAR |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Vchild - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Pchild - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Korpro - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Onepro - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| VCHILDVCHILD |
	| PCHILDPCHILD |
	| KORPROKORPRO |
	| ONEPROONEPRO |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Korpro - ${staticCompanyName} |

Scenario: Add partner
	Testing the ability to create a regular project in Dossiera and add the project partner in the provisioning page account details 

	Given I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	And I generate a provisioning company name
	And I generate a provisioning project name
	And I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message on sandbox with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Contact Role                           | Liferay Account Customer Role              |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay DXP Production                     |
	| Project Name                           | Korpro - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	And I update a postal address on koroneiki for the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" with the street address "456 Fake Street" to have the following values
	| Primary | True |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" to the following roles
	| Support Developer |
	And I update a koroneiki account with the name "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" to have the following values
	| Tier | Regular |
	And I create a team role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the partner role |
	| Name        | Partner                  |
	| Type        | Account                  |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORPARKORPAR                                   |
	| Contact Email Address | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken           |
	| Description           | Test provisioning partner account on koroneiki |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-9012                                   |
	| Name                  | Korpar - ${staticCompanyName}                  |
	| Profile Email Address | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken           |
	| Region                | United States                                  |
	| Status                | Approved                                       |
	| Tier                  | Regular                                        |
	| Website               | www.koroneikipartner.com                       |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product with the following values
	| Name | Service Partnership | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korpar - ${staticCompanyName}" and the product "Service Partnership" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Perpetual   | true     | |
	| Quantity    | 1        | |
	| Status      | Approved | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "kwSgiajslgb7ecsD"
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Details" tab
	And I edit the following account fields and types to the following values under the account details tab
	| Partner/Reseller/SI | Select Entity | Korpar - ${staticCompanyName} | |
	| First Line Support  | Select Entity | Korpar - ${staticCompanyName} | |
	Then I should be able to view the following account values in the account details page
	| Name           | Korpro - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Code           | KORPROKORPRO                  |
	| Status         | APPROVED                      |
	| Support Region | United States                 |
	| Country        | United States                 |
	| SLA            | Platinum                      |
	| Developers     | 1 / 3 Filled                  |
	| Tier           | Regular                       |
	| Partner        | Korpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	Then I should be able to view the following account values under the account details tab
	| Account Name        | Korpro - ${staticCompanyName} | |
	| Status              | APPROVED                      | |
	| Code                | KORPROKORPRO                  | |
	| Tier                | Regular                       | |
	| Partner/Reseller/SI | Korpar - ${staticCompanyName} |	|
	| First Line Support  | Korpar - ${staticCompanyName} |	|
	| Street 1            | 456 Fake Street               | |
	| Country             | United States                 | |
	| City                | Diamond Bar                   | |
	| State/Province      | California                    | |
	| Postal Code         | 91765                         | |
	| Primary             | Yes                           | |
	| Dossiera Account    | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}   | |
	| Salesforce Project  | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey} | |
	When I click on the "Support" tab
	Then I should be able to view the following account values under the account details tab
	| Support Region | United States | |
	And the team with the name "Korpar - ${staticCompanyName}" assigned the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" should have the team role "Partner"
	And the team with the name "Korpar - ${staticCompanyName}" assigned the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" should have the team role "First Line Support"
	And the team with the name "Koroneiki Partner" assigned the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" should not have the team role "Partner"
	When I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	Then I should be able to view an account on the provisioning index with the name "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" and the following values
	| Name    | Korpro - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Code    | KORPROKORPRO                  |
	| Partner | Korpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Region  | United States                 |
	| SLA     | Platinum                      |
	| Tier    | Regular                       |
	| Status  | APPROVED                      |
	When I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "History" tab
	And I generate the account ID value for "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}"
	Then the history entry in position number "1" with the field value "contactEmailAddress" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account                 |
	| Update Field Name           | contactEmailAddress                  |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And the history entry in position number "1" with the field value "internal" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account |
	| Update Field Name           | internal             |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | false                |
	And the history entry in position number "1" with the field value "code" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account |
	| Update Field Name           | code                 |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | KORPROKORPRO         |
	And the history entry in position number "1" with the field value "region" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account |
	| Update Field Name           | region               |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | United States        |
	And the history entry in position number "1" with the field value "parentAccountId" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account |
	| Update Field Name           | parentAccountId      |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | 0                    |
	And the history entry in position number "1" with the field value "accountId" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account |
	| Update Field Name           | accountId            |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticAccountId}   |
	And the history entry in position number "1" with the field value "name" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account          |
	| Update Field Name           | name                          |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | Korpro - ${staticCompanyName} |
	And the history entry in position number "1" with the field value "status" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Account |
	| Update Field Name           | status               |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | Approved             |
	And the history entry in position number "12" with the field value "tier" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Koroneiki Admin > Updated Account |
	| Update Field Name           | tier                              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                               |
	| Update Field New Value      | Regular                           |
	And the history entry in position number "13" with the field value "Team Role" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Test Test > Assigned Team > Korpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Update Field Name           | Team Role                                                 |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                       |
	| Update Field New Value      | Partner                                                   |
	And the history entry in position number "14" with the field value "Team Role" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Test Test > Assigned Team > Korpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Update Field Name           | Team Role                                                 |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                       |
	| Update Field New Value      | First Line Support                                        |

